; A barrier between a 64-bit increment and a 64-bit load.
;
; The increment's old value is dropped, so it takes the 64-bit reduction form that
; already existed. The load is the pair read as one value, which needs the warp
; target — and the barrier used to keep the module away from it, because a single
; thread running 32 lanes has no second lane to arrive with. The warp target now
; runs the lanes in step: one program counter each, and the lowest one is run
; first, so a lane parked on the barrier cannot be passed by a lane that has not
; arrived.
;
; That makes the barrier observable rather than decorative. Every lane of the one
; warp adds one, waits, then loads: if the barrier holds, all 32 lanes read the
; same number — the counter after all 32 increments — and every slot ends up with
; that value. If it did not hold, the first lanes to arrive would read a smaller
; counter than the last ones, and the slots would disagree with each other.
               OpCapability Kernel
               OpCapability Addresses
               OpCapability Int64
               OpCapability Int64Atomics
               OpMemoryModel Physical64 OpenCL
               OpEntryPoint Kernel %main "atom64bar" %gid
               OpName %main "atom64bar"
               OpDecorate %gid BuiltIn GlobalInvocationId
       %void = OpTypeVoid
        %u32 = OpTypeInt 32 0
        %u64 = OpTypeInt 64 0
       %u64p = OpTypePointer CrossWorkgroup %u64
     %v3u64 = OpTypeVector %u64 3
       %pin = OpTypePointer Input %v3u64
       %fnty = OpTypeFunction %void %u64p %u64p
        %gid = OpVariable %pin Input
        %scp = OpConstant %u32 1
        %sem = OpConstant %u32 0
        %one = OpConstant %u64 1
       %main = OpFunction %void None %fnty
         %a0 = OpFunctionParameter %u64p
         %a1 = OpFunctionParameter %u64p
      %entry = OpLabel
       %bump = OpAtomicIAdd %u64 %a0 %scp %sem %one
                OpControlBarrier %scp %scp %sem
        %now = OpAtomicLoad %u64 %a0 %scp %sem
          %g = OpLoad %v3u64 %gid
         %gi = OpCompositeExtract %u64 %g 0
         %pa = OpPtrAccessChain %u64p %a1 %gi
                OpStore %pa %now
                OpReturn
                OpFunctionEnd
